config ZMK_BLE_LINK_POLICY
    bool "Prioritize the selected BLE HID host connection"
    depends on ZMK_BLE && BT_PERIPHERAL
    depends on !ZMK_SPLIT || ZMK_SPLIT_ROLE_CENTRAL
    default n
    help
      The selected BLE HID endpoint requests the configured peripheral
      preference. Other known host links request latency 30, including while
      application data is transferred. USB means no selected BLE HID host.
      Split links, unknown hosts and other local identities are excluded.
      Does not change bonds, advertising, PHY, packet sizes or supervision
      timeout. Remote hosts decide actual parameters; requests are bounded
      and event driven.

config ZMK_BLE_SPLIT_POLICY
    bool "Adapt the outgoing split interval to activity"
    depends on ZMK_SPLIT_BLE && ZMK_SPLIT_ROLE_CENTRAL && BT_CENTRAL
    depends on ZMK_SPLIT_BLE_CENTRAL_PERIPHERALS = 1
    default n
    help
      Independently manage the single outgoing central-role split link.
      ACTIVE uses ZMK's normal split preference; IDLE uses the interval
      below. Preserve the normal split latency and supervision timeout.
      SLEEP schedules no further requests. Host profiles and their selected
      endpoint policy are separate and are never promoted by this policy.
      Requires exactly one configured split peer; ambiguous actual central
      links are rejected. No heap, new thread or periodic settled-idle work.

config ZMK_BLE_SPLIT_POLICY_IDLE_INTERVAL
    int "Idle split interval (1.25 ms units)"
    depends on ZMK_BLE_SPLIT_POLICY
    range 7 48
    default 24
    help
      24 is 30 ms. This must exceed ZMK_SPLIT_BLE_PREF_INT and satisfy
      the supervision-timeout bound with ZMK's preferred latency/timeout.
      Compilation checks both constraints. Peers may refuse the request;
      an accepted request is not proof of applied radio parameters.

config ZMK_BLE_LINK_POLICY_LOG_LEVEL
    int "BLE link policy log level"
    range 0 4
    default 3
    help
      Numeric slot and connection-parameter observations only; no addresses,
      input values, message contents or authentication data.

config ZMK_BLE_LINK_POLICY_DIAGNOSTICS
    bool "Record bounded link worker and API wall times"
    depends on ZMK_BLE_LINK_POLICY && LOG
    default n
    help
      Emit one numeric linkwork record after a worker that issued a request.
      Records worker/API wall time, request count, logical host mask, selected
      slot and pending delay. No payload, address, heap, new thread or timer.
      Clock samples use the system cycle counter and exclude the final summary
      log's own cost. This is not CPU, radio airtime or host HID delivery timing.
